## Summary

I've created:

1. **`Selector.vue`** - A reusable single/multiple selection component with:
   - Text filtering with real-time search
   - Alphabetical sorting of items
   - Support for both single and multiple selection modes
   - Avatar display for items
   - Selection badges

2. **`ChatLLMModelSelector.vue`** - Uses Selector for LLM models (single selection)

3. **`ChatProfileSelector.vue`** - Rewritten to use Selector for profiles (multiple selection)

4. **`ChatInputBox.vue`** - New unified input component that:
   - Places LLM model selector before profile selector
   - Manages the editor and toolbars
   - Removed model selector from toolbar

5. **`ChatInputToolbar.vue`** - Simplified toolbar (removed LLM selector)

6. **`Chat.vue`** - Updated to use new ChatInputBox component

All components follow the VueDeveloper profile structure with proper TailwindCSS styling and DaisyUI components.

I'll fix the selectors to display full width. The issue is that the selector buttons need to expand to fill available space.

